    "historical_decision": "The sovereign state admitted to the U.N. in 1960 continued through successive official names: Republic of the Congo (Léopoldville), Democratic Republic of the Congo from 1 August 1964, Republic of Zaire from 27 October 1971, and Democratic Republic of the Congo again from 17 May 1997. U.N. authority records explicitly describe each transition as a name change. ATLAS therefore models one continuous polity identity rather than separate state extinctions/replacements.",
    "activity_rule": "Patrice Lumumba's sovereign-state premiership, Moïse Tshombe's continuous 10 July 1964–13 October 1965 premiership, and Mobutu Sese Seko's continuous 25 November 1965–16 May 1997 presidency all belong to the same DRC polity identity. Official-name changes must not split continuous office tenures.",
    "designation_rule": "Preserve Republic of the Congo (Léopoldville) / 콩고 공화국(레오폴드빌) as official_name from independence on 30 June 1960 through 31 July 1964. Preserve Republic of Zaire / 자이르 공화국 as official_name from 27 October 1971 through 16 May 1997."
